From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:19:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(context): collapse older relayed agent messages

context.collapse_agent_messages (false = off): a hub's relayed agent message ([Agent message am_... from ...]) in a user row before the current turn keeps its header line and body, and its instructions paragraph (about 500 chars, repeated in every such message) becomes a one-line note with the same facts: who wrote it, never the user's approval, how to answer. Applies on the wire and to the compaction summarizer's input; the turn that reads a message still gets it whole.
